data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` into a `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work exactly like any other unmanaged type with `stackalloc`:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[4];
```

On this 64-bit system each element is 8 bytes. The only gotcha is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context since the size isn't fixed at compile time — but `stackalloc` itself works in safe code when assigned directly to a `Span`.
